# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: cadgui-4-crx-api — CRX: an ARX/BRX-like C/C++ extension ABI
#+STATUS: DEFERRED
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: feature
#+DEPENDS: cadgui-2-qt6-gui-host cadgui-action-layer
#+TARGET: release 3.0
#+BRANCH: qt6-gui
#+DATE: 2026-11-16
#+PARENT: cadgui-release-3.0-epic

* Context

Phase 4 of [[cadgui-release-3.0-epic]]. A versioned C/C++ extension ABI so native
plug-ins (dll/dylib/so) extend cadgui like ObjectARX/BRX extend AutoCAD/BricsCAD.

REALITY (scope-honest): a binary drop-in of real ARX/BRX is impossible -- their
ABI is bound to their internal C++. *CRX is an ARX-LIKE OWN ABI*, so the target
is SOURCE portability: recompile a plug-in against CRX headers. This phase
delivers the 2D object-model API; 3D entity APIs extend it in phases 5-6, so the
ABI is versioned + extensible from the start.

* Foundation

The in-process C boundary already built in phase 2 (slice F: display-list pull +
input + repaint, [[cadgui-2-qt6-gui-host]]) is the SEED of CRX. CRX generalises
it into a full, documented, versioned SDK. Every CRX command / custom entity
registers through the [[cadgui-action-layer]] registry, so native extensions are
AI-driveable and guard-checked too.

* Deliverables

- A versioned C/C++ ABI: entity / command / selection / prompt / transaction /
  reactor / custom-object surfaces.
- The loader (dll/dylib/so) + lifecycle.
- The C-ABI <-> cador marshalling layer.
- The CL extension API (AutoLISP + vlax, extended) as the Lisp-side peer.
- Headers + samples + SDK documentation; a reference sample plug-in.

* Dependencies / sequencing

After phase 2's C boundary and the Action Layer. Design the ABI ONCE, right
(versioned, extensible for 3D) -- this is the expertise-bound bit where a human
C-ABI architect most repays. Independent of the 2D breadth of phase 3.

* Test & doc approach

- A reference sample plug-in compiled against the CRX headers, loaded, and driven
  headless through the Action Layer (round-trip: register a CRX command -> invoke
  it -> assert its effect).
- ABI compatibility tests across a version bump.
- Doc: the CRX SDK reference (headers + guide + samples).

* Acceptance themes

- [ ] A sample C/C++ plug-in compiles against CRX headers, loads into cadgui, and
      registers a command + a custom entity.
- [ ] The CRX command is invokable + introspectable via the Action Layer.
- [ ] Entity/selection/prompt/transaction/reactor surfaces exercised by samples.
- [ ] A later ABI version loads the prior sample (versioning holds).
